      "text": "Dana Okonkwo\nMechanical & Design Engineer\ndana@example.org · +351 900 000 000 · https://danaokonkwo.example\nSummary\nMechanical engineer on single-use medical devices, from sketch to tooling release; EU patent holder.\nExperience\nDesign Engineer\nHydra Medical · Mar 2023 – Present · Lisbon\nLed the dose-counter redesign on a 400,000-unit-a-year inhaler: nine parts down to five, two weeks off the tooling schedule.\nBuilt the team’s drop and cycle test rig and wrote its verification protocols.\nQualified two moulding suppliers, one in Portugal and one in Poland, and ran the first-article inspections.\nBuilt the tolerance stack for the counter mechanism and caught a 0.3 mm interference before the first tool was cut.\nPrototyping Technician\nPolytechnic Prototyping Lab · Sep 2021 – Feb 2023 · Porto\nRan a seven-machine prototyping shop: four FDM printers, a resin printer, a benchtop mill and a laser cutter.\nKept the shop’s machines running: logged and fixed about 300 faults a year, most of them within a day.\nClean-room Technician\nMedisure Contract Manufacturing · Jun 2018 – Dec 2020 · Porto\nCut scrap on the balloon-bonding line from 6% to 2.5% by redesigning the bonding fixture.\nSet up SPC charts on the two highest-scrap stations and trained the line leads to read them.\nRan the validation build for a new catheter line: installation, operational and performance qualification on 11 stations.\nEducation\nM.Eng. Mechanical Engineering · Universidade do Porto · 2021",
