      "text": "Dana Okonkwo\nMechanical & Design Engineer\ndana@example.org · +351 900 000 000 · https://danaokonkwo.example\nSummary\nMechanical engineer working on single-use medical devices from first sketch to tooling release; EU patent holder. Spent three years on the clean-room side of a contract manufacturer before moving into design.\nExperience\nDesign Engineer\nHydra Medical · Mar 2023 – Present · Lisbon\nLed the dose-counter redesign on an inhaler running 400,000 units a year; cut the part count from nine to five.\nBuilt the drop and cycle test rig the team now uses for design verification, and wrote the test protocols that go with it.\nRan the weekly DFM reviews with the toolmaker through three rounds of T1 samples, closing 41 of 44 issues before tooling release.\nPrototyping Technician\nPolytechnic Prototyping Lab · Sep 2021 – Feb 2023 · Porto\nRan a seven-machine prototyping shop: four FDM printers, a resin printer, a benchtop mill and a laser cutter.\nClean-room Technician\nMedisure Contract Manufacturing · Jun 2018 – Dec 2020 · Porto\nRan ISO 7 clean-room assembly for three catheter products, about 9,000 units a week across two shifts.\nCut scrap on the balloon-bonding line from 6% to 2.5% by redesigning the bonding fixture.\nEducation\nM.Eng. Mechanical Engineering · Universidade do Porto · 2021",
