      "text": "Dana Okonkwo\nMechanical & Design Engineer\ndana@example.org\nExperience\nPrototyping Technician\nPolytechnic Prototyping Lab · Sep 2021 – Feb 2023 · Porto\nRan a seven-machine prototyping shop: four FDM printers, a resin printer, a benchtop mill and a laser cutter.\nTaught the machine-safety induction to about 120 students a year and wrote the handbook for it.\nDesigned and printed over 60 jigs and fixtures for student capstone projects, from drill guides to a vacuum-forming frame.\nKept the shop’s machines running: logged and fixed about 300 faults a year, most of them within a day.\nWrote the lab’s equipment grant application: €48,000 for a five-axis mill, approved on first submission.\nFreelance CAD Designer\nSelf-employed · Jan 2021 – Aug 2021 · Remote\nCAD and rendering for two small furniture studios, including the assembly drawings they shipped with the product.\nBuilt a searchable parts library for one studio so their joiners could find hardware by fixing type and load.\nClean-room Technician\nMedisure Contract Manufacturing · Jun 2018 – Dec 2020 · Porto\nRan ISO 7 clean-room assembly for three catheter products, about 9,000 units a week across two shifts.\nCut scrap on the balloon-bonding line from 6% to 2.5% by redesigning the bonding fixture.\nSet up SPC charts on the two highest-scrap stations and trained the line leads to read them.\nRan the validation build for a new catheter line: installation, operational and performance qualification on 11 stations.\nWrote or rewrote 22 work instructions after a customer audit, all accepted without findings at the follow-up.\nDesign Intern\nAtelier Norte · Jun 2017 – Sep 2017 · Porto\nModelled and rendered an eight-piece outdoor furniture range for the studio’s trade-fair catalogue.\nEducation\nM.Eng. Mechanical Engineering\nUniversidade do Porto\nOther\nDriving licence, category B"
    }
